{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויכירם", :translit "va'yakireim", :gloss "and he recognized them"} {:he "ויתנכר אליהם", :translit "va'yitnaker aleihem", :gloss "and he made himself strange to them"} {:he "ויכר", :translit "va'yar", :gloss "and he recognized"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between plural ויכירם and singular ויכר explained by the intervention of the angel"}], :frame {:text "Genesis 37:15 records that 'a man found him [Joseph] wandering in the field' (Genesis 37:15). The man is identified as the angel Gabriel in Bereshit Rabbah 84:14–15. Joseph here in Genesis 42:7 initially sought to greet his brothers warmly but was reminded by this angel of his prophetic mission, causing him to conceal his recognition.", :sources ["Genesis 37:15" "Genesis 42:7" "Bereshit Rabbah 84:14–15"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויתנכר", :translit "va'yitnaker", :gloss "and he made himself strange"} {:he "על ידי האיש גבריאל", :translit "al yedei ha'ish gavriel", :gloss "by the hand of the man Gabriel"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויתנכר", :b "על ידי האיש גבריאל"}], :frame {:text "Genesis 37:15 describes 'a man' who found Joseph wandering; the midrash in Bereshit Rabbah 84:14–15 identifies this man as the angel Gabriel. The phrase 'the man Gabriel' (האיש גבריאל) echoes that identification, linking Joseph's act of estrangement directly to angelic intervention.", :sources ["Genesis 37:15" "Bereshit Rabbah 84:14–15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between plural ויכירם and singular ויכר explained by the intervention of the angel", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ויתנכר", :a-value 686, :b "על ידי האיש גבריאל", :b-value 686, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:11:13.575560806Z", :model "glm-5.2"}